  "narrative": {
    "summaryIntro": "Grishneshwar Temple, located near Aurangabad in Maharashtra, is the southernmost and youngest among the twelve Jyotirlingas. Dedicated to Lord Shiva as Grishneshwar, the temple is situated near the UNESCO World Heritage Site of Ellora Caves, one of India's most important archaeological treasures. The temple features Hemadpanti architectural style, characteristic of medieval Maharashtra.\n\nThe temple holds immense historical and spiritual significance as a major pilgrimage destination. Located in a region rich with Buddhist, Hindu, and Jain monastic caves, the temple represents the continuity of Hindu spirituality. The site attracts both religious pilgrims and heritage tourists interested in India's ancient civilizations and architectural traditions.",
